e0$ let $d_{\lambda\mu}:=[C^{\lambda}:D^{\mu}]$ be the multiplicity of $D^{\mu}$ as a composition factor of $C^{\lambda}$ (well defined by [[thm-jordan-holder-theorem-for-modules]] and [[def-composition-series-and-length-of-a-module]]). Then $$d_{\mu\mu}=1\qquad	ext{and}\qquad d_{\lambda\mu}
e0\ \Longrightarrow\ \lambda\unrhd\mu,$$ i.e. a nonzero off-diagonal entry can occur only in the allowed direction of the cell order $\unrhd$ (larger cell first). Equivalently, after any linear extension of $\unrhd$ and with rows $\lambda\in\Lambda$ and columns $\mu$ such that $D^{\mu}
e0$, the decomposition matrix of $A$ is lower unitriangular. This determines only the diagonal and the vanishing region: no off-diagonal entry is computed by cellularity.
